#: ../recording.rst:288
msgid "Where Recordings Are Saved"
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:290
msgid "Recordings are saved in the project's assets folder under ``recordings``. If the project has not been saved yet, OpenShot uses its user-data location. Filenames contain the source name and a timestamp; another numeric suffix avoids overwriting a file created during the same second."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:294
msgid "Save the project before a long or important session so its recording destination is predictable. Do not move or rename recorded files outside OpenShot while the project is using them."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:298
msgid "Permissions and Platform Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:300
msgid "Screen and camera capture depend on operating-system services, hardware, and build support. The controls in the dock adapt to the available backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:303
msgid "**Linux/X11:** Full-screen, window, and numeric region capture are available when the X11 capture backend is built."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:304
msgid "**Linux/Wayland:** The desktop sharing portal chooses the capture source after recording starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:305
msgid "**Windows:** Desktop capture uses the available Windows screen backend; camera devices use Windows capture services."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:306
msgid "**macOS:** Screen capture uses the supported macOS backend, with window and region choices represented as cropped screen bounds when required. System Audio recording is not currently supported; microphone recording remains available as a separate audio source."
msgstr ""

#: ../recording.rst:310
msgid "The first recording may trigger Screen Recording, Microphone, Camera, or desktop-sharing permission prompts. Approve the requested source, then restart OpenShot if the operating system requires it. A disabled source card or option is preferable to a recording that silently omits an unsupported source."
msgstr ""

